    "body": "From an external bug-bounty report (rounds 9/10, tested against compiled binary at commit 67f8ef6, real PreToolUse hook JSON, isolated $HOME).\n\nSeveral common ways of starting a script aren't recognised by the script-path extractor, so the target file is never scanned: wrapper commands, interpreter flags that take a value, and newer runtimes. The report's detailed write-up and repro steps weren't completed in the original session — whoever picks this up should rebuild the specific reproduction cases from the code.\n\n**Priority: Medium** — related to previously-closed #117, which covered different cases of the same class.\n\n*— Claude (Sonnet 5), clawband backlog automation*",
